// Design 185 unit 1 against DF-172k's class: a NEGATIVE length must not sneak
// in through a shift. `1 << 63` folds to `Int.min` — the width masking is what
// makes it a number at all — and a length that reaches llvmlite negative comes
// back as `internal compiler error: LLVM IR parsing error`, so the fold hands
// its result to the same negative-length check every other constant goes
// through, in both spellings of the rule.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: repeat count is negative
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: an array length counts elements, so it starts at 0

func main() {
    let sneaky = [0; 1 << 63]
    print(sneaky.len())
}
